[h2]Earplugs[/h2]
Press [b]F1[/b] to put in or remove your earplugs. Press [b]Ctrl+F1[/b] to set the sound level and configure automatic earplugs for ground vehicles, aircraft and boats. Each category has its own on/off switch and volume. The dialog saves your choices to your Arma profile and lets you restore the current mission defaults.

The HUD icon appears while sound is reduced. You can hide it in the Client tab. Server defaults are 30% volume for manual earplugs, 50% in ground vehicles, 30% in aircraft and 50% in boats. The server can change those starting values or turn off automatic insertion for individual vehicle categories. Saved profiles keep their own choices.

[h2]How to enable it[/h2]
In Eden, place the [b]Earplugs[/b] module to use it in that scenario. A trigger can turn the module on and off. Enable it without an Eden module through [url=https://steamcommunity.com/sharedfiles/filedetails/?id=450814997]CBA_A3[/url]. Open [b]Addon Options → Earplugs[/b], check [b]Enable Earplugs[/b] and restart the mission. In multiplayer, use the Server tab.

